+### 2348 — An EMPTY environment filter is a decision, and needs a negative to be load-bearing
+- FINDING: gemini, muse and agy strip NOTHING. All three are `withSpawnEnv(os.Environ(), cfg)` in the source — no `filterEnv`, no codex-family strip, no PATH sanitization — so their children inherit `CLAUDECODE`, the whole `CODEX_*` family, both service URLs, the credentials their pointers name, and the board credentials `BUG-260819-3qn52o` records. Gemini is the extreme case of that bug's general shape: its filter names nobody, so it leaks from every direction at once.
+- DECISION: Each of the three keeps an `env.go` whose only code is `WithRunContext`, because an empty filter expressed by omitting the file is indistinguishable from a port that forgot — especially for a reader arriving from qwen's twelve-key filter one directory over.
+- FINDING: The parity package's two permanent negatives do NOT transfer to these three. A prefix strip has no exact-key strip to be a near miss OF here, so the attack collapses into something else while pretending to measure a rule. The bound that actually bites is the opposite defect — a plugin that HAS a filter — so each carries `TestABorrowedRuntimeFilterFailsAgainstThe<X>Golden`, which bolts the shared codex-family strip onto the real plugin and requires the golden to fail, plus a narrowing showing the codex-family keys in `parent_env` are what catches it.
