+- FINDING: `--add-dir` was in agy's argv signature until the guard reported the CODEX plugin's own `Args`. Codex spells it too, to hand its child the board directory (source `adapter.go:332`). The literal is still in agy's real argv; it is simply not evidence that a function is spelling AGY argv, and it is now excluded with the residual it leaves demonstrated staying open.
+- NOTE: This is the cross-plugin false-positive test doing exactly what it exists for, on the first task where five siblings existed to measure against. The rule the claude port wrote down — check every candidate literal against the OTHER agents' builders before adopting it — was applied by hand for `--dangerously-skip-permissions` and `--output-format` and still missed this one. The test found what the reading did not.
+- DECISION: Every new plugin's guard now scans all five sibling packages rather than one, so the next collision is reported rather than argued about.
