+### 2342 — An aliasing test that lets the append reallocate proves nothing
+- ROOT CAUSE: `TestArgsDoesNotAliasTheCallersPrefix` was written as "mutate `args[0]`, check the caller's `prefix[0]`", with a prefix of len 2 cap 8. qwen's `Args` appends EIGHT arguments, so the append overflowed the capacity, Go reallocated, and the aliasing plugin looked correct. The mutation harness caught it: the "prefix not copied" mutant was the one survivor of the first run.
+- FIX: The test now asserts against the caller's BACKING ARRAY — a 64-element array of sentinels with a two-element window handed over — so an aliasing plugin is caught whatever the capacity arithmetic does. Added to all four new plugins, and all four mutants are now caught.
+- NOTE: The claude version of this test passes only because its `Args` appends few enough arguments to stay inside the capacity. It is correct today by arithmetic, not by construction.
