+### 2136 — A refusal probe that varies one field too many proves the WRONG rule
+- ROOT CAUSE: A negative case is only evidence for the rule it names if that rule is the ONLY one that can refuse it. `claude/composition.go` validates each server against several rules in sequence; four of its refusals had a named case that tripped an EARLIER rule, so the named refusal was never executed and deleting it left the whole suite green. This is the third recurrence of the shape recorded at 2026-08-22 2132 (the codex unknown-field probe that substituted a field FOR the url and was refused by the transport rule instead).
+- FINDING: Mutating EVERY refusal branch and sub-condition in `composition.go`, rather than reading for the pattern, found nine unbound branches where review had identified two. Four were shadows — unknown-server, duplicate-server, unnamed-server, and `entry.Type != server.Transport` — and five were sub-conditions with no case at all (http with no url, http with args, stdio with headers, stdio with no command, `root.MCPServers == nil`). A targeted re-read of the two the reviewer named would have left seven in place.
+- FINDING: The shadowing mechanism is worth naming because it will recur: an undeclared server name resolves to the ZERO `CompositionServer`, whose `Transport` is `""`. Any probe that names a transport therefore disagrees with that zero value and is refused by the per-transport rule BEFORE the existence check runs. The same zero-value effect shadows the unnamed-server rule, and the "last declaration wins the map" effect shadows the duplicate rule whenever the probe also varies the transport.
+- DECISION: Each isolating probe is built by varying only the field its rule reads: `"type":""` for the existence rule, an identical transport with a differing `BearerTokenEnvVar` for the duplicate rule, a matching whitespace key on both sides for the name rule, and an entry valid under the metadata's own shape with only `type` flipped for the transport-equality rule. The rule is now stated in `TestTheCompositionValidatorRefuses`'s doc comment, with a per-case comment saying what must not be "tidied" back.
+- NOTE: The duplicate case's shape matters beyond the mutant. Varying the transport tests nothing; varying the CREDENTIAL is the dangerous form — a reviewer reading the first declaration believes the child reads `REVIEWED`, the map keeps the last, and the child reads `SNEAKY`.
+- NOTE: A capability field is not pinned by being declared with a comment saying it may not move. `Capabilities.HomeEnvVar`/`DefaultHome` carried exactly that comment and both moved silently through the whole suite; codex pinned the identical pair and caught it. On-disk limit state is keyed by the home these resolve to.
+- SCOPE: `pkg/agentic/systems/claude/composition_test.go`, `claude_test.go`, `args_test.go`. No production behaviour changed: 21 mutants, 21 caught, 0 survivors.
