+### 2325 — Goal-mode launch preparation cannot live behind any plugin method
+- DECISION: The claude port carries goal mode's ARGV half and explicitly leaves its PREPARATION half out of the plan surface. `pkg/agentic/systems/claude/goal.go` states the whole of what the source does there.
+- FINDING: `PrepareClaudeGoalLaunch` (source, `spawn/claude_goal.go`) does four things before construction: validates the board goal contract, gates on Claude Code >= 2.1.139 by running `claude --version`, probes `/goal` capability by running `claude -p --output-format json /goal`, and decides a session action (`native_goal_bound` / `binding_retained` / `successor_required`). Steps two and three START PROCESSES. `BuildPlan` calls EVERY `System` method to build a DRY RUN, so preparation behind `ResolveBinary`, `Argv` or `Stdin` would make a dry run execute the harness twice — the exact drift this repo's dry-run-as-a-mode design exists to prevent. Step four is not a plan fact at all: it decides about a session that already exists, which the source itself records by making `ClaudeGoalBinding.Rollback` a documented no-op.
+- DECISION: One piece of preparation IS carried across — the refusal of a goal whose provider condition is empty. Without it a goal-bound launch ships the literal argument `/goal ` and the child is told it is bound to nothing, with no error anywhere. A validating gate must not get weaker across a move; this repo has recorded that failure once already, on `CompositionServer.BearerTokenEnvVar`.
+- NOTE: Home for the rest is the launch/session plane when that is ported, in the position `PreflightClaudeGoalLaunch` holds in the source's command layer. This task invents no home for it.
